    {
      "repository": "elayadesign/ai-design-skills",
      "url": "https://github.com/elayadesign/ai-design-skills",
      "trending_rank": 1,
      "description": "A collection of design skills for AI coding tools: Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, Windsurf and anything that reads a Markdown rules file. It currently holds one skill, landing-page-design, a 19 KB SKILL.md that takes ==a landing page from intake questions to a shipped page==: page structure, conversion copy, SEO, and a visual system for type, spacing, corner radius, motion and states, ending in a checklist.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list, and GitHub's top entry today. Unlike tool-backed design checkers, it is ==one plain Markdown file you can read in full== before trusting it, and it installs by copying that file, with no scripts, hooks or downloads in the repository. Its design values (fonts, colours, spacing, motion) sit in one section, so a team can fork it and set its own house style.",
      "caveat": "It is ==a single skill so far==: a design-to-motion skill added on 25 October moved to a separate repository two days later, and the redesign skill lives in another. The guidance is one designer's opinions, including a mandatory tagline-reveal section, and adapts parts of the MIT-licensed taste-skill. GitHub shows no language because the repository is Markdown only, and there are no releases or tests. We did not use it.",
      "category": "Design / AI coding",
      "language": null,
      "license": "MIT",
