    {
      "repository": "obra/superpowers",
      "url": "https://github.com/obra/superpowers",
      "trending_rank": 4,
      "description": "An ==agentic skills framework and development methodology== for coding agents such as Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI and Antigravity: skills that walk the agent through brainstorming a design, writing a plan, test-driven implementation, subagent-driven execution and code review, installed as a plugin from official marketplaces or from this repository.",
      "why_interesting": "Back on our list after our 17 October card, because v7.0.1 (21 October) changed its core behaviour. Building on the brainstorming rebuilt in v7.0.0, it now reads your project before asking anything and ==writes a design doc before building==; the maintainers say this cut skipped docs in one test scenario from 24 of 24 runs to 3 of 24. It also trimmed long skills below Claude Code's 20,000-character cut-off after compaction, after one session lost its five-round fix limit.",
      "caveat": "More questions and design docs add latency and token cost, and the maintainers say they are still tuning brainstorming. The test figures come from their own scenario, not an independent benchmark. Installation differs per harness, the optional visual companion has telemetry you can switch off, and the project ==no longer accepts agent-written PRs== for other people's issues unless a maintainer asks. We did not install or test it.",
      "category": "AI coding / developer workflow",
